{"text": "Home.\n\nRavi stands up. There is a small green ferry. It goes to the other side.\n\n\"Can I come, please?\" asks Ravi.\n\nA kind woman smiles. \"Yes, you can.\"\n\nThe ferry goes over the river. The wind is in Ravi's hair. He can see the white boat. The kite is still on it.\n\nSoon they are on the other side. Ravi jumps off. He runs near the river.\n\nThe white boat stops, too. Ravi can see the red kite.\n\n\"Please! My kite!\" calls Ravi.\n\nThen the town clock rings. One, two, three… twelve.\n\nAnd the wind turns.\n\nThe kite goes up into the sky. Now it flies back over the river!\n\n\"No!\" says Ravi. \"Not again!\"\n\nRavi runs after the kite again. Here there is a long bridge. He runs over it.\n\nThe kite flies over the market. Mr Das sees Ravi. He laughs. \"The wind turns at twelve!\"\n\nThe kite flies up the hill. Ravi runs up the hill, too. His legs are very tired.\n\nHe knows this street. He knows this tree. He knows this house.\n\nIt is his street!\n\nThe red kite is in some flowers. They are on a small balcony.\n\nIt is Ravi's balcony!\n\nMum is there. She holds the red kite. She laughs.\n\n\"Ravi! Your kite is home first!\"\n\nRavi laughs, too. He is tired, hot and very happy. He thinks of Mr Das.\n\nThe morning wind goes to the river. At twelve, it turns. It brings the kite home.\n\nMum looks at the clock. It is twelve o'clock.\n\n\"Lunch is ready,\" she says.", "textSha256": "cb106b3988bf2cf75752b5d2d94b74737c5e513696b5e030e5c36e7b12b70c44", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.9, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["H", "o", "m", "e", ".", "\n", "\n", "R", "a", "v", "i", " ", "s", "t", "a", "n", "d", "s", " ", "u", "p", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "a", " ", "s", "m", "a", "l", "l", " ", "g", "r", "e", "e", "n", " ", "f", "e", "r", "r", "y", ".", " ", "I", "t", " ", "g", "o", "e", "s", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "o", "t", "h", "e", "r", " ", "s", "i